NAME
       pkg - package manager

SYNOPSIS
       **pkg** __operation__ [__options__] [__targets__]

DESCRIPTION
       **pkg** installs, removes and updates software packaged for PureC OS. It
       works like **pacman**: a package is an archive (**name-version-arch.pkg.tar.gz**),
       repositories are plain files (a database plus packages) on a web server,
       and the list of installed packages lives in **/var/lib/pkg/local**.

       Changing operations need root rights.

OPERATIONS
       **-S** __names__
              install packages and the packages they depend on from the repositories.
              **-Sy** first downloads fresh package databases, **-Su** upgrades every
              package that has a newer version in a repository, **-Syu** does both
              (like **pacman -Syu**): it shows the list and asks before changing anything.
       **-Ss** __text__   search names and descriptions in the repositories
       **-Si** __name__   information about a repository package
       **-Sl** [__repo__] list repository packages
       **-Sc**        delete cached package files that are not installed
       **-R** __names__   remove packages. A package that another one needs is not removed
              (see **--nodeps**). **-Rs** also removes the dependencies that were
              installed only for them and nothing else needs.
       **-Q** [__names__]  list installed packages. **-Qi** information, **-Ql** files,
              **-Qo** __file__ the owner of a file, **-Qe** explicitly installed, **-Qd** installed
              as a dependency, **-Qs** __text__ search, **-Qu** packages with an update in the
              databases, **-Qk** check that the files exist, **-Qq** names only
       **-U** __files__   install package files from disk
       **-D** __names__   change the install reason: **--asdeps** or **--asexplicit**

OPTIONS
       **--root** __dir__    work on another root directory (databases, files and
                      the configuration are all taken under it)
       **--config** __file__ use another configuration file
       **--noconfirm**  do not ask questions
       **--needed**     do not reinstall a package that is up to date
       **--force**      overwrite files that exist but belong to no package
       **--nodeps**     do not check dependencies (**-Rd** is the same for removal)
       **--asdeps**, **--asexplicit**
                      set the install reason
       **-v**, **--version**

CONFIGURATION
       **/etc/pkg.conf** has an **[options]** section (**Architecture**, **SigLevel**) and one
       section per repository with one or more **Server** lines. **$repo** and **$arch** in
       an address are replaced. An address is a web address (the **curl** program is used)
       or **file:///path** / **/path** for a directory.

           [options]
           SigLevel = Optional

           [ports]
           Server = https://example.org/purec/$arch

       **SigLevel** is **Never** (no check), **Optional** (a signature is checked when the
       repository has one, a bad one is always refused) or **Required**. The database
       is signed with ECDSA P-256; the public keys are the files **/etc/pkg/keys/*.pub**
       (65 bytes, as hexadecimal text). Packages are checked by the SHA-512 sum in the
       signed database.

PACKAGES
       Files listed in **backup** of a package are configuration files. When an upgrade
       finds such a file changed by you, your file stays and the new one is written next
       to it as **name.pkgnew**; when a package is removed a changed file is kept as
       **name.pkgsave**. A package can carry scripts that run through **/bin/sh** with
       **PKG_ROOT**, **PKG_NAME**, **PKG_VERSION** and **PKG_OLD_VERSION** set:
       **post-install**, **post-upgrade**, **pre-remove**, **post-remove**.

FILES
       /etc/pkg.conf, /etc/pkg/keys/, /var/lib/pkg/local/, /var/lib/pkg/sync/,
       /var/cache/pkg/

SEE ALSO
       curl(1), sync(1)
